{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeMeasure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeMeasure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.EqHaar","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.WithDensity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ImproperIntegrals"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.integral_Ioi_hemisphere","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.integral_Ioi_hemisphere","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L306-L317","doc":"The same integral at the **hemisphere height** `z₀ = √(R² - d²)`, which is\nthe form H4 actually consumes: over a base point at distance `d` from the centre\nof a hemisphere of radius `R`, the vertical fibre contributes\n`1 / (2(R² - d²))`.\n\nSumming this over the base triangle is what produces the Λ-sum; that summation\nis H4-2/H4-3 and is NOT done here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.integral_Ioi_rpow_neg_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.integral_Ioi_rpow_neg_three","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L294-L304","doc":"**The vertical hyperbolic integral converges**, with the elementary value\n`∫_{z₀}^{∞} z^{-3} dz = 1/(2 z₀²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L260-L281","doc":"**H2 (horizontal translation) — `hypVolume` is invariant under `p ↦ v + p`\nwhenever `v` has zero height.**\n\nThe `v 2 = 0` hypothesis is essential and not a technicality: a *vertical*\ntranslation genuinely changes hyperbolic volume (it is not an isometry of `H³`),\nso the density's dependence on `z` is exactly what must be protected here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L253-L258","doc":"A translation that fixes the height leaves the density unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_smul","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L191-L243","doc":"**H2 (dilation) — `hypVolume` is invariant under `p ↦ r • p` for `r > 0`.**\n\nThe `λ³` from Lebesgue and the `1/λ³` from the density cancel. Proved by\ntransporting the integral along `Measure.map_addHaar_smul`, which is available\nonly because the carrier is `Fin 3 → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_smul","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L182-L189","doc":"Scaling pulls a clean factor out of the density: `1/(λz)³ = (1/λ³)·(1/z³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_compl_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_compl_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L165-L170","doc":"**The complement of `H³` is `hypVolume`-null.**  The measure is genuinely a\nmeasure ON the upper half-space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L153-L163","doc":"The density vanishes off the upper half-space, so `hypVolume` is supported\non `H³` with no cutoff needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity_pos","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L146-L151","doc":"The density is strictly positive on the upper half-space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_apply","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L128-L134","doc":"**The hyperbolic volume measure** `dV = dx dy dz / z³` on the upper\nhalf-space model.\n\nThe name records the intent; the JUSTIFICATION that this is the hyperbolic\nvolume is the invariance package H2 (`qou-5gai`), not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurable_hypDensity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurable_hypDensity","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L123-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypDensity","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L117-L121","doc":"The hyperbolic density `1/z³`.  Outside the upper half-space `z ≤ 0`, where\n`ENNReal.ofReal` sends the (non-positive) value to `0` -- so the measure below\nis automatically supported on `H³` rather than needing a cutoff. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_upperHalfSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_upperHalfSpace","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L114-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_upperHalfSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.isOpen_upperHalfSpace","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L111-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.upperHalfSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.upperHalfSpace","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeMeasure.lean#L107-L109","doc":"**Upper half-space**, the domain of the `H³` model: points of `ℝ³` with\npositive last coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}